 "says": "Ana founds a Team whose policy has no admission rule, which returns her membership by founding and the founding epoch, and configures a Google connection expecting the hd claim example.com. Ben signs in through it for admission on his own device; the owner verifies the callback and returns sign-in evidence, and the callback also carried his address ben@example.com. None of this admits him: Ana's membership change naming the connection, the policy in force and Ben's verified evidence is refused by the owner with claim_not_admitted. A policy that would admit by e-mail domain is refused at admission (no such claim can be written), a provider-claim membership that names no admitting policy is refused at admission, and a device-key binding that tries to carry Ben's e-mail as an identity is refused at admission. What must not happen: any membership record, policy version or binding being committed from a verified login or a matching e-mail domain alone.",
